SELECT
  skills_dim.skills,
  COUNT(skills_job_dim.job_id) AS demand_count,
  ROUND(AVG(salary_year_avg), 0) AS Top_paying_skills
FROM
  job_postings_fact
  INNER JOIN
    skills_job_dim ON job_postings_fact.job_id = skills_job_dim.job_id
  INNER JOIN
    skills_dim ON skills_job_dim.skill_id = skills_dim.skill_id
WHERE
  job_postings_fact.job_title_short = 'Data Analyst'
 AND salary_year_avg IS NOT NULL
 AND job_work_from_home = TRUE
GROUP BY
  skills_dim.skills
ORDER BY
  Top_paying_skills DESC
LIMIT 25;

High Demand for Big Data & ML Skills: Top salaries are commanded by analysts skilled in big data processing (PySpark, Couchbase), machine learning tools (DataRobot, Jupyter), and core Python data libraries (Pandas, NumPy), reflecting a high market premium on advanced modeling and large-scale data manipulation.

Software Development & Deployment Proficiency: Knowledge of version control, CI/CD, and orchestration tools (Bitbucket, GitLab, Kubernetes, Airflow, Jenkins) indicates a lucrative overlap with data engineering and DevOps, where automation and reliable pipeline management drive significant value.

Cloud Computing & Modern Data Platforms: Expertise across cloud-based analytics environments and data infrastructure (Databricks, GCP, Elasticsearch, PostgreSQL) underscores that enterprise migration to distributed cloud architectures directly boosts an analyst’s earning potential.